# Docker build context.
#
# Only `backend/` and `ai/` are COPY'd by Dockerfile.backend, and only
# `frontend/` by Dockerfile.frontend — but the whole repo is shipped as the
# build context, so this list decides what the daemon sends and what lands
# inside the image.
#
# Two entries here are load-bearing rather than cosmetic:
#
#   **/node_modules  Dockerfile.frontend's build stage does
#                    `COPY frontend/ ./` AFTER `COPY --from=deps .../node_modules`.
#                    Without this exclusion the host's node_modules (Windows
#                    .node binaries on a Windows dev box) would silently
#                    overwrite the Linux ones and `npm run build` would fail
#                    at runtime with an architecture mismatch.
#
#   backend/data     a local dev SQLite DB (sentinelai.db + -wal + -shm)
#                    must never be baked into a shipped image.
#
# .env is also excluded as belt-and-braces: no COPY statement reaches the repo
# root, but secrets should not be inside the build context at all.

.git
.github

# --- secrets / local state -------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
backend/data
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- host-specific binaries and caches ------------------------------------
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.venv
venv

# --- dev-only artifacts ----------------------------------------------------
frontend/test-results
frontend/playwright-report
frontend/coverage
docs
scripts
